\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1 The main things to be concerned with in the image above is Center, Middle, OuterMiddle, and Suburban. There is where you place your building prefabs. See step 5a and up to add buildings as it requires more setup than just adding them to the array. Also the density. If you leave it at 1 that's the highest density. As you get closer to 30 the density of the buildings approches none. So if you used 15 that would give you about half the buildings that 1 gives. The District multiplier is applied to all districts. Center, Middle, OuterMiddle, and Suburban. A higher number makes each district bigger. So if you don't see certain buildings spawning from a certain district then maybe you should lower your district multiplier. Or if the districts look too small raise it.\par
step4. Adjust map size(Make sure Gizmos is selected in the editor). About 100 is a good size for a 2K terrain. \par

