\tab Notice in the image there are 3 lines and a blue sphere. Use the distance from road slider and watch the 3 lines move away from the building. The 3 lines represent the road and the grey lines are supposed to be the edges of the road whereas the yellow line is the center of the road. Use the Y Roatation Offset to move the blue sphere. Whereever the blue sphere faces is going to be the front side of your building. If it's not moving adjust the Z value of size on the BuildingType Component. You must have skipped a step if it doesn't move.\par
\par
step5i Under Buildings remove all buildings you don't want in each array labeled as Center, Middle, Outter Middle, and Suburban. This is in the Graph Generator we dragged into the scene ealier.\par
\tab step5j Add the building to the array you want. All arrays have to have at least 1 building.\par
\par
Step6. Select the Graph generator in your scene.\par
\par
Step7. Notice there is a wire cube gizmo. Make sure it is over the terrain where you want the City to Spawn. You can drag it over the terrain.\par
\tab Step7a You can also adjust the terrain steepness with a slider. If you slide it to 100 Roads will be very steep. If you slide it closer to 0 roads will be more level.\par
\par
\par
Step8. Play around with the Max Minor Roads and Max Major Roads to get different looking cities. in the City Generator Component.\par
\par
Step9. Click Build Roads. This should be almost instantly finished after you click the button.\par
\par
\par
step10. Click your road spline if it hasn't automatically done so for you. You need to do this so it will apply the road settings.\par
Step 11. Click Place Buildings. Depending on your heightmap settings and your iterations in the smooth component this could take a couple minutes to hours. And keep in mind if you have more than 1 terrain that time is multiplied by the number of terrains that you have active. For a 2K terrain generated by Gaia Pro 2021 with a heightmap resolution of 4097 and 400 iterations it will take around an hour to complete that job. Keep in mind that lowering that heightmap resolution to 1025 or possibly lower would speed that up to just take a few minutes.\par
\par
step 12. If you have Gaia you can generate a Biome now.\par
\par
Addition info. If you don't want to generate the roads you can just use Gena Pro to make your road as usual and make your roads manually. Just when you're done refer to step 11. Also I recommend a road width of 22 because it's what everything else goes by.\par
